    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1018">

                <pb facs="0885" n="769" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg769"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/3416.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the American Ambassador</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-30T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 30, 1912—6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Great fear at Durango that in case Federal soldiers are withdrawn that place will
                    be at mercy of bandit bands. Request that sufficient troops be retained
                    adequately to protect Americans and American interests at Durango.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
